* **ui:** per-fleet configuration column and dashboard rows ([#11](https://github.com/stanvx/ci-runner-farm/issues/11) M3, M4) ([#18](https://github.com/stanvx/ci-runner-farm/issues/18)) ([70bab2d](https://github.com/stanvx/ci-runner-farm/commit/70bab2dd7c3eecd5bb2e52401b5a21728309a745))
* **ui:** security posture, three status cards, richer runner table ([#11](https://github.com/stanvx/ci-runner-farm/issues/11) M2) ([#17](https://github.com/stanvx/ci-runner-farm/issues/17)) ([d043c9f](https://github.com/stanvx/ci-runner-farm/commit/d043c9fa6f79641bbf6672469bfa1e8eab14202d))
* **ui:** settings-page facelift — tabbed fleet hub, image builder, cache/stats, native theming ([#33](https://github.com/stanvx/ci-runner-farm/issues/33)) ([fc95b61](https://github.com/stanvx/ci-runner-farm/commit/fc95b614c61dc8dca99c68358e67ea428c4a0297))
### Bug Fixes
* **autoscale:** reap disconnected (health=unhealthy) runners, not just exited ([#25](https://github.com/stanvx/ci-runner-farm/issues/25)) ([727e4e2](https://github.com/stanvx/ci-runner-farm/commit/727e4e2ed0aaf5753f40c82e64e586c5bb7cd1b3))
* **dind:** real-FS Docker data root for runners + FUSE cache-root guard/warning ([#7](https://github.com/stanvx/ci-runner-farm/issues/7)) ([1f06c8e](https://github.com/stanvx/ci-runner-farm/commit/1f06c8e508d0c537b16e08a91bf773beeb61b9c3))
* honor EPHEMERAL=false, enforce autoscale MIN floor, runner-owned cache dirs ([#30](https://github.com/stanvx/ci-runner-farm/issues/30)) ([a605b80](https://github.com/stanvx/ci-runner-farm/commit/a605b80193cd93ba37ee9849c8ea52ba3110cd45))
* land stranded review fixes and release public CA readiness (1.5.0) ([#19](https://github.com/stanvx/ci-runner-farm/issues/19)) ([5acc848](https://github.com/stanvx/ci-runner-farm/commit/5acc8484fdfc08a399a8d315eadf1d999408c2ee))
* **plugin:** dedicated .tgz package + Unraid config idioms ([#23](https://github.com/stanvx/ci-runner-farm/issues/23)) ([97873dc](https://github.com/stanvx/ci-runner-farm/commit/97873dc377e2bea6a46af95f976e45951f17b880))
* recreate runners with a fresh token instead of resurrecting stale ones ([#22](https://github.com/stanvx/ci-runner-farm/issues/22)) ([411d5cd](https://github.com/stanvx/ci-runner-farm/commit/411d5cd5f24f6602684df8d60148d2807da1d4a2))
* **release:** credit commit authors in notes ([#35](https://github.com/stanvx/ci-runner-farm/issues/35)) ([7307817](https://github.com/stanvx/ci-runner-farm/commit/73078170d2156559b928b30d86e9bf677f857bda))
* **release:** update release-please action ([#38](https://github.com/stanvx/ci-runner-farm/issues/38)) ([4a33381](https://github.com/stanvx/ci-runner-farm/commit/4a333817291f452a9cb46ea7782334cdca0054d0))
* scope install extraction to plugin dir, force root perms ([bb869cc](https://github.com/stanvx/ci-runner-farm/commit/bb869cc7ee266d55795c5b59ade4044a752679cf))
* **ui:** keep the fleet log panel visible when empty ([#4](https://github.com/stanvx/ci-runner-farm/issues/4)) ([79e032d](https://github.com/stanvx/ci-runner-farm/commit/79e032d13bf92a2bd30ca4e1c49b9d1417d522a3))
* **ui:** load jquery.filetree js+css so the Cache root picker actually works ([e352946](https://github.com/stanvx/ci-runner-farm/commit/e352946d43197d5ab2be8dc69585abe8642ca0ac))
* **ui:** use Unraid native inline help (markdown form + :plug:/&gt;/:end) ([43c52b3](https://github.com/stanvx/ci-runner-farm/commit/43c52b323d6ed58a6bee813eae7b24b72a1f208f))
</CHANGES>

<!-- plugin package: Unraid downloads it to flash and verifies the MD5 -->
<FILE Name="&cfgdir;/&packageName;">
<URL>&packageURL;</URL>
<MD5>&packageMD5;</MD5>
</FILE>

<!-- install (entities are NOT expanded inside CDATA, so use literal paths) -->
<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE><![CDATA[
set -e
PLGDIR="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/ci-runner-farm"
CFGDIR="/boot/config/plugins/ci-runner-farm"
mkdir -p "$CFGDIR" "$PLGDIR"
# Sweep any older package versions off flash, keeping this build's package.
find "$CFGDIR" -maxdepth 1 -name 'ci-runner-farm-*.tgz' ! -name 'ci-runner-farm-2026.07.26.0854.6-1.8.0.tgz' -delete 2>/dev/null || true
# Extract ONLY into the plugin dir; --no-same-owner forces root ownership;
# --no-overwrite-dir leaves existing dir metadata alone. System dirs untouched.
# The .tgz is kept on flash so the on-boot reinstall works without a download.
tar -xzf "$CFGDIR/ci-runner-farm-2026.07.26.0854.6-1.8.0.tgz" --no-same-owner --no-overwrite-dir -C "$PLGDIR"
chown -R root:root "$PLGDIR"
find "$PLGDIR" -type d -exec chmod 0755 {} +
find "$PLGDIR" -type f -exec chmod 0644 {} +
chmod 0755 "$PLGDIR/include/runner-farm.sh"
[ -d "$PLGDIR/nchan" ] && find "$PLGDIR/nchan" -type f -exec chmod 0755 {} +
# Unraid's emhttp_event executes these on Docker service start/stop — must be +x
[ -d "$PLGDIR/event" ] && find "$PLGDIR/event" -type f -exec chmod 0755 {} +
# Config defaults are NOT seeded to flash — the settings page and runner-farm.sh
# both fall back to built-in defaults, so flash only ever holds what the user set.
[ -f "$CFGDIR/Dockerfile" ] || cp "$PLGDIR/default.Dockerfile" "$CFGDIR/Dockerfile"
# Migrate saved Dockerfiles seeded before the cache-ownership fix: without
# runner-owned CACHE_MOUNTS destinations baked into the image, Docker's
# bind-mount auto-creation leaves root-owned parents and a non-root runner
# fails writing beside them (rustup: "could not create bin directory
# '/home/runner/.cargo/bin'"). Patch only files that still carry the stock
# packages marker and lack the fix; customized files without the marker get a
# notice instead.
DF="$CFGDIR/Dockerfile"
if [ -f "$DF" ] && ! grep -q 'mkdir -p /home/runner/.cargo/registry' "$DF"; then
  if grep -q '^#  && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/\*' "$DF"; then
    BLK=$(mktemp)
    cat > "$BLK" <<'EOF_CACHEDIRS'

# Pre-create the default CACHE_MOUNTS destinations as runner-owned. When these
# paths are absent from the image, Docker's bind-mount auto-creation makes the
# missing parent directories root-owned, and a non-root runner (RUN_AS_ROOT=false)
# can then no longer write beside them — e.g. rustup fails with "could not
# create bin directory '/home/runner/.cargo/bin': Permission denied".
RUN mkdir -p /home/runner/.cargo/registry /home/runner/.cargo/git \
      /home/runner/.cache/sccache /home/runner/.cache/yarn /home/runner/.cache/ms-playwright \
      /home/runner/.npm /home/runner/.local/share/pnpm/store \
 && chown -R runner:runner /home/runner/.cargo /home/runner/.cache /home/runner/.npm /home/runner/.local
EOF_CACHEDIRS
    sed -i "\@^#  && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/\*@r $BLK" "$DF"
    rm -f "$BLK"
    echo "ci-runner-farm: patched saved Dockerfile to pre-create runner-owned cache dirs (press Build to rebuild the runner image)."
  else
    echo "ci-runner-farm: NOTE - saved $DF lacks the runner-owned cache-dir block from default.Dockerfile; merge it manually so non-root runners can write beside the cache mounts."
  fi
fi
( docker pull myoung34/github-runner:latest >/dev/null 2>&1 & ) || true
# Bring the fleet + autoscaler up. Runs on manual install AND on every boot
# (rc.local reinstalls plugins), detached so it waits for dockerd+array without
# blocking. No-op until a GitHub token is configured.
( nohup "$PLGDIR/include/runner-farm.sh" boot-autostart >>"$CFGDIR/boot.log" 2>&1 & ) || true
echo ""
echo "+=============================================================+"
echo "| ci-runner-farm 2026.07.26.0854.6-1.8.0 installed.                         "
echo "| Settings > Utilities > CI Runner Farm                        "
echo "| Set a GitHub PAT, then Start (or Validate without a token).  "
echo "+=============================================================+"
]]></INLINE>
</FILE>

<!-- remove -->
<FILE Run="/bin/bash" Method="remove">
<INLINE><![CDATA[
PLGDIR="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/ci-runner-farm"
CFGDIR="/boot/config/plugins/ci-runner-farm"
"$PLGDIR/include/runner-farm.sh" stop 2>/dev/null || true
rm -rf "$PLGDIR"
# The downloaded package is just a cache; drop it. Config + token stay.
rm -f "$CFGDIR"/ci-runner-farm-*.tgz
echo "ci-runner-farm removed. Config + token left in /boot/config/plugins/ci-runner-farm (delete manually to purge)."
]]></INLINE>
</FILE>

</PLUGIN>
